rt controls that these officers would monitor and enforce."},{"industry":"defense","confidence":0.8,"rationale":"Defense and aerospace manufacturers export controlled items subject to the Export Administration Regulations that this program would oversee."},{"industry":"manufacturing","confidence":0.65,"rationale":"Industrial manufacturers exporting dual-use goods and controlled equipment would be subject to enhanced monitoring under this program."}],"plainSummary":"This bill creates a formal five-year program within the Commerce Department to station at least 20 export control officers at U.S. embassies and consulates abroad. These officers would monitor whether exports comply with U.S. regulations and help detect illegal diversions of controlled goods to unauthorized users or countries. The bill also requires the appointment of a director to run the program.","classificationMethod":"llm","plain":{"whoItTouches":"Anyone who buys imported goods, and people who make goods here.","confidence":"crs-summary"},"topOverlap":{"bioguideId":"L000582","score":0.034653761621182416},"overlapCount":12},"meaning":{"percentile":6.436346426881212,"median":0.01073720309570498,"n":6339,"ordinary":[],"unattributedShare":0.681113084905792}}],"votes":[{"id":"a64a90b759595d68f3a8d502","billId":"119-hr-7008","date":"2026-07-22T16:51:00-04:00","question":"Yea-and-Nay","result":"Passed","position":"Yea","sourceUrl":"https://clerk.house.gov/evs/2026/roll280.xml"},{"id":"2afa499bcaceefdcecfa862a","billId":"119-hr-8800","date":"2026-07-22T16:37:00-04:00","question":"Yea-and-Nay","result":"Passed","position":"Yea","sourceUrl":"https://clerk.house.gov/evs/2026/roll278.xml"},{"id":"e69a4fe10a0cc4e4d35ffc3d","billId":"119-hr-6955","date":"2026-07-21T22:05:00-04:00","question":"Yea-and-Nay","result":"Passed","position":"Yea","sourceUrl":"https://clerk.house.gov/evs/2026/roll271.xml"},{"id":"c68077c5b6dd6fe8eb42bf43","billId":"119-hres-1438","date":"2026-07-21T14:39:00-04:00","question":"Recorded Vot